92186421526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421526 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421526 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421526 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421526 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8e5fe0f3-2bfd-5489-af0f-1a776954c9bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421527 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fe4e956c-1b1f-5312-af0b-3bb85188fdbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421528 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421528 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74609" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421528 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421528 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨2,-6,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,-7,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421528 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b9c3557-0777-5517-a4eb-de326b8ca141" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421528 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=3 \\\\ 4s-6t=-7 \\\\ 3s-4t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=3 \\\\ 2t=5 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=5\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =3 \\\\ -s+2(\\frac{5}{2}) & =3 \\\\ -s+5 & =3 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=\\frac{5}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+\\frac{5}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421529 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421529 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421529 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421529 #edb/ref 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421529 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9fca2b37-ca0d-5f9c-9cd0-c84b2660c1c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421529 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-5.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(-5)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=20.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{a}_{1}+(-5){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 20\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+(-5)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=20\\cdot (-5)=-100.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421530 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421530 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105215" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421530 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421530 #edb/ref 1071 "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421530 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c75c18ab-94b6-560b-bd47-66c76f099710" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421530 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=1,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $b$ does *not* lie in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421531 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421531 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105242" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421531 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421531 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421531 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cdba03e5-45ad-5856-b84f-f9bccefe0c86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421531 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+39{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 18 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+19.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+19\\,⇒\\,k=-19.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421532 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421532 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421532 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421532 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421532 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6e087fb-be43-5d06-8b0f-af7c87178067" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421532 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-8{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -12{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -12 & -6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-9\\,⇒\\,k=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
